49,3,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
50,3,1,talk,May,,"The options are Rotating Location, Managed Collection Hours, or an Enclosed Structure. I'm leaning away from the structure.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Given the smell and the maintenance fights Midori mentioned, the Enclosed Structure is a bad idea.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"I don't want a huge bill. Rotating seems cheapest, but @Servas mentioned the paperwork is a hassle.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Managed Hours sounds like it would lead to the ""policing"" I fear. Rotating seems more naturally fair.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Rotating requires notice for every change, but it prevents one person from bearing the entire burden.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,May,,"@Midori, if we rotate, the person with the narrow frontage still has to deal with it. Is that okay?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,It's better than one person dealing with it forever. Managed Hours is too restrictive with that early truck.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Kenji,,I vote for Rotating. It's the most budget-friendly for everyone.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Midori,,I agree with Kenji. It's better to share the annoyance than to fight over a schedule.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Servas,,"I concur. A rotating burden is a shared burden, which is more philosophical and fair.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,May,,I'll go with Rotating too. It's the only way to ensure the gate owner gets a break.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,I'm also voting for Rotating. It avoids the smell of a bin house and the stress of a strict window.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
